SOUND SAMPLES (V ROM)
=====================

Raw and processed audio samples for the YM2610 ADPCM-A and ADPCM-B channels.

DIRECTORY LAYOUT
----------------
  in_wav_a/        — Source WAV files for ADPCM-A (6-channel samples)
  in_wav_a_voice/  — Source WAV files for generated ADPCM-A voice samples
  in_wav_b/        — Source WAV files for ADPCM-B (delta-T streaming)
  out_16el_a/      — Intermediate 16-bit LE WAVs for ADPCM-A
  out_16el_a_voice/— Intermediate 16-bit LE WAVs for voice samples
  out_16el_b/      — Intermediate 16-bit LE WAVs for ADPCM-B
  out_a/           — Final .adpcma encoded files
  out_a_voice/     — Final .adpcma voice files packed after regular SFX
  out_b/           — Final .adpcmb encoded files
  downloads/       — Downloaded raw sample sources

ENCODING PIPELINE
-----------------
1. Place WAV source files in in_wav_a/ (ADPCM-A), in_wav_a_voice/
   (ADPCM-A voice bank), or in_wav_b/ (ADPCM-B).
2. Run: make samples
   (runs the ADPCM-A, voice, and ADPCM-B conversion steps)
3. Run: make vrom
   (packs all .adpcm* files into 777-v1.v1, regenerates sample_table.inc,
   and writes sdk/sound_voice_ids.h)

SAMPLE INDICES
--------------
vrom.py generates sound/driver/sample_table.inc automatically.

  ADPCM-A regular SFX: index 0-11 -> playSFX(n)
  ADPCM-A voice bank:  generated SOUND_VOICE_* constants -> speakText(),
                       playVoiceSample(), playVoiceWord(), playVoiceNumber()
  ADPCM-B streams:     index 0-8 -> playSFXB(n)

The SDK automatically switches ADPCM-A samples above 63 to the parameterized
driver command, so generated voice IDs can be passed directly.

Current ADPCM-B live roles:

  0 = title theme
  1 = stage loop 1
  2 = stage loop 2
  3 = ending / results theme

ADPCM-A VOLUME
--------------
Per-channel TL register (port B, regs $08-$0D):
  Bits 7:6 = pan (11 = both speakers)
  Bits 5:0 = TL attenuation (0 = max volume, 63 = silent, 0.75 dB/step)
Driver default: $C0 = pan both, TL=0 (maximum volume).

AUTO-STOP
---------
The driver uses software timers to cut ADPCM-A playback and prevent noise tails.
To adjust: edit the adpcma_stop_ticks table in sound/driver/driver.asm.
